# #86: sleeping skips the night in the Mortal Realm (life/sleep.js) and in the Tensura world (vanilla). Expect no "ttl:" failure lines, and in the log
# "[ttl] sleep: the night was slept away in ttl:mortal_realm". The Mortal Realm reads the overworld's clock and vanilla
# never wrote a night slept away there back to it: the sleepers were woken and it stayed night.
# A fresh bot starts Life 1 in the Mortal Realm; it is the only soul there, so it alone is the 50 %.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSleep
@sleep 4
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep expect mortal
time set 18000
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep bed
# Vanilla waits until the sleeper has slept 100 ticks (5 s), then the morning comes.
@until 20 ttl sleep expect morning
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep expect awake
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep clear
# The Tensura world (vanilla's own overworld sleep, same 50 % rule): reborn, the soul sleeps there too.
kill TtlBotSleep
execute as TtlBotSleep run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotSleep run ttl choose slime
@sleep 3
time set 18000
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep bed
@until 20 ttl sleep expect morning
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep expect awake
ttl sleep TtlBotSleep clear
ttl reset TtlBotSleep
ttlbot remove TtlBotSleep
